                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It just isn't fun to me, and I don't think it will be fun to a lot of others. FYI: I received this in a bundle with some other games that I wanted, so I figured I'd try this out,\n\nThis is the entire singleplayer game: use the radar in the bottom left to find the enemy, CHASE the enemy around (they never even shoot at you), shoot the enemy a few times, kill the enemy, find the next enemy, chase and kill, get an upgrade, kill the enemy, etc. The just isn't a lot to the game to make it fun, from my view. \n\nThe multiplayer, and maybe the entire game, appears to have been made in an attempt to jump on the agar.io/slither.io/tank.io popularity, but has unfortunately failed that mainly due to a lack of players. I know developers can't just make more people play the game, but they can do two things:\nAdd bots that can actually shoot at you! Having actual combat between players and bots would make this 10x better.\nSecond, improve on the overall gameplay: make it more fun. I don't know if they were going for minimalistic combat, but that's what it is.\n\nPros: Menu is unique, but needs polishing. Soundstracks/sound effects are good and match the aesthetic. There is a noticable learning curve that helps you get through the game, which I like. I haven't had any performance issues besides a few second freeze when restarting the level.\nMultiplayer seems like it will be fun, but I need some other people or bots to actually tell.\n\nFinally, this is definitely overpriced. Maybe if the features I mentioned were fixed/added it could be at the current price, but right now I couldn't see this going for more than $5.\n\nThose are my thoughts on the game. When I have some free time and I don't feel like playing other games, I'll try this one some more. My review could change based on my future gameplay, so I hope the developer won't give up on this game. Thanks for reading.",
